From 8e4127024d86cbf0279dd3f1623b3f7396ac92b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jackie grey <leftstick22@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 23:18:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add FAULT_BUFFER netlist device for runtime fault
 injection

Adds a transparent buffer with a runtime MODE parameter that lets the
Arcade Cabinet Fault Simulator project inject the four primary digital
fault primitives at any instrumented pin:

  MODE 0 = NORMAL    (Y follows A; default pass-through)
  MODE 1 = STUCK_HI  (Y driven high regardless of A)
  MODE 2 = STUCK_LO  (Y driven low  regardless of A)
  MODE 3 = OPEN      (Y high-impedance; pin appears disconnected)

Implementation reuses MAME's existing tristate_output_t pattern from
nld_74125.cpp, so the netlist solver does not need any FAULT_BUFFER-aware
code paths. Auto-instrumentation will insert one FAULT_BUFFER per
fault-eligible pin in a separate preprocessor pass.

Verified end-to-end with nltool against tests/netlist/fault_buffer_test.cpp:
all four modes produce the expected output signatures.

Files changed:
  src/lib/netlist/devices/nld_fault_buffer.cpp   (new device)
  scripts/src/netlist.lua                        (add to build)
  src/lib/netlist/generated/nld_devinc.h         (FAULT_BUFFER macro)
  src/lib/netlist/generated/lib_entries.hxx      (LIB_ENTRY)

Co-Authored-By: Oz <oz-agent@warp.dev>
